  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "the-thread",
      "text": "Let's zoom out. Everything you've learned serves one engine: empiricism — transparency, inspection, adaptation. The artifacts make work transparent. The events are our regular inspections. And every event ends by adapting something: Planning adapts the plan, the Daily adapts the day, the Review adapts the Product Backlog, and the Retrospective adapts how we work. That's the whole machine.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "draw": [
            {
              "t": "card",
              "id": "pillars",
              "x": 120,
              "y": 110,
              "w": 400,
              "h": 70,
              "text": "Transparency · Inspection · Adaptation",
              "color": "green"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "draw": [
            {
              "t": "note",
              "x": 120,
              "y": 210,
              "text": "Artifacts → transparency · Events → inspection · Outcomes → adaptation"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "anti-patterns",
      "text": "Now let me protect you from the traps I see most often. Extending a Sprint because work isn't done — no; the box is fixed. Running the Daily as a status report to a manager — no; it's the Developers' re-plan. Treating the Scrum Master as a project manager or note-taker — no; they're a coach. A Product Owner who is really a committee — no; one person decides. No Definition of Done — then 'Done' means nothing. Velocity as a target — and your data starts lying. Skipping the Retrospective — and you stop improving. Spot these, and you're already ahead of most teams.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "draw": [
            {
              "t": "card",
              "id": "ap1",
              "x": 40,
              "y": 110,
              "w": 250,
              "h": 60,
              "text": "Extending the Sprint",
              "color": "red"
            },
            {
              "t": "card",
              "id": "fix1",
              "x": 360,
              "y": 110,
              "w": 260,
              "h": 60,
              "text": "Fixed box; move work to backlog",
              "color": "green"
            },
            {
