    {
      "id": "end-to-end",
      "text": "Let's try it together. Imagine a two-week Sprint. On day one you set a Sprint Goal and pick items within your velocity. Each morning, a fifteen-minute Daily keeps you honest against a burndown. Something's blocked — the Scrum Master clears it. At the end, you show a Done, usable Increment at the Review and gather feedback, then run a Retrospective and pick one improvement. Do that, Sprint after Sprint, living the five values — and that's Scrum working. Ready for the final check?",
      "steps": [
        {
          "draw": [
            {
              "t": "note",
              "x": 110,
              "y": 150,
              "text": "Goal → pick within velocity → Daily + burndown → Review → Retrospective → repeat"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
